     "result_text_tail": "he removal line. The deck recommends raising the trigger to 20% and running a store test first.\n- **The $40M goal:** no route reaches $40M by 2030 within the limits. Amazon-led reaches about $26M in 2030, and about $40M around 2032 if it keeps growing ~29% a year.\n\n**What the deck asks the board to decide:**\n- Approve the first stage, which needs $1.9\u20132.9M of cash in 2027.\n- Adopt ad-cost checkpoints for early 2028: continue as planned at 28% or less, continue with a spending freeze at 28\u201334%, cut back above 34%.\n- Decide in advance whether a 1\u20132 year payback delay is acceptable in the middle case.\n- Restate the $40M goal as a path to about 2032.\n- Replace the store trigger with the stricter one above.\n\n**Choices I made where I would have asked you** (all listed on appendix slide 19):\n- **\"On the way to $40M by 2030\":** I read it as a direction rather than a hard 2030 target, since no option reaches $40M by then.\n- **Awareness:** I used 4% among all skincare buyers. Using 9% among K-beauty buyers gives the same result.\n- **Inventory:** stock is four months of landed product cost, with the build-up counted as cash out.\n- **One-off costs:** store fixtures and launch fees are counted as costs in the year they occur.\n- **Tariff:** if the duty rises to 25%, I assumed it takes effect from mid-2027.\n- **Japan:** the scale-up is treated as extra on top of the group's existing plan.\n- **Market size:** I used $3.6B, not the $5.2B trade-press figure, which includes makeup and hair care."
    }
